@TB-022 @gateway
Feature: Gateway keeps the correlation id and propagates the trace
  As an operator
  I want every request to carry one consistent correlation id from client through gateway to service
  So that I can follow a request across services when debugging without trusting the client-supplied value

  Background:
    Given a fake upstream is running
    And the gateway is configured to point at the fake upstream

  # Notation in the Examples table: "a*64" is the character a repeated 64 times; (empty) is a header with an empty value;
  # (not sent) means the header is absent; "\t" is a tab character; "\\" is one backslash.
  @S01 @FR-003
  Scenario Outline: A valid id is preserved, a missing id is generated by the gateway
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with X-Correlation-Id <id>
    Then the fake upstream and the response get exactly the same single correlation id
    And that correlation id is <outcome>

    Examples:
      | id            | outcome     |
      | "abc-123_X.9" | "preserved" |
      | "a*64"        | "preserved" |
      | (not sent)    | "new GUID"  |

  @S02 @FR-003 @NFR-006
  Scenario Outline: An invalid id is replaced with a new id
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with X-Correlation-Id <id>
    Then the fake upstream and the response get exactly the same single correlation id
    And that correlation id is "new GUID"

    Examples:
      | id                    |
      | "a b"                 |
      | "id;drop"             |
      | "<script>"            |
      | "a*65"                |
      | (empty)               |
      | "abc\n"               |
      | (arabic-indic digits) |
      | "a\tb"                |
      | "a[b"                 |
      | "a\\b"                |
      | "a^b"                 |
      | "a`b"                 |
      | "a/b"                 |
      | "a@b"                 |
      | "a{b"                 |

  @S08 @FR-003
  Scenario: Two X-Correlation-Id values are treated as invalid
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with two X-Correlation-Id headers "abc" and "def"
    Then the fake upstream and the response get exactly the same single correlation id
    And that correlation id is "new GUID"

  @S10 @FR-003
  Scenario Outline: Every method gets exactly one X-Correlation-Id in the response
    When I send "<method>" to "<path>" with X-Correlation-Id "client-id-m"
    Then the fake upstream and the response get exactly the same single correlation id
    And the response has exactly one X-Correlation-Id header equal to "client-id-m"

    Examples:
      | method | path              |
      | HEAD   | /api/v1/boards    |
      | POST   | /api/v1/boards    |
      | DELETE | /api/v1/boards/42 |

  @S03 @FR-003
  Scenario: The client traceparent is propagated to the upstream in the same trace
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with a valid traceparent
    Then the fake upstream receives a traceparent with the same trace id as the client but a different span id

  @S11 @FR-003
  Scenario: Without a traceparent the upstream still receives a valid traceparent of a new trace
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards"
    Then the fake upstream receives a valid traceparent

  @S12 @FR-003
  Scenario: A malformed traceparent is ignored and the gateway starts a new trace
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with traceparent "00-not-valid-01"
    Then the status code is 200
    And the fake upstream receives a valid traceparent different from the value the client sent

  @S04 @FR-001
  Scenario: A 404 carries a correlationId equal to the response header
    When I send "GET" to "/no-such-route" with X-Correlation-Id "client-id-404"
    Then the response is 404 problem+json with code "ROUTE_NOT_FOUND"
    And the correlationId in the body equals the X-Correlation-Id header of the response
    And the response has exactly one X-Correlation-Id header equal to "client-id-404"

  @S09 @FR-003
  Scenario: The health endpoint also returns X-Correlation-Id
    When I send "GET" to "/health/live"
    Then the response has exactly one X-Correlation-Id header that is a GUID

  @S07 @FR-003
  Scenario: An id returned by the upstream does not give the response two values
    Given the fake upstream always returns X-Correlation-Id "from-upstream"
    When I send "GET" to "/api/v1/boards" with X-Correlation-Id "client-id-1"
    Then the response has exactly one X-Correlation-Id header equal to "client-id-1"
